The runner had already exited on its OWN after the stop file ('no further cycle' at 23:53:59Z), so this
call is a no-op by design. Nothing was killed: no Stop-Process, no taskkill, no key sent to any window.

## THE CENSUS -- over ALL processes of ANY exe, not only python
  denominator                              : 555 processes examined
  matching 'cycle_runner|backfill_driver'  : 0    <- the order requires NONE
  POSITIVE CONTROL (same instrument, same field, a string that IS live):
    matching 'inbox-watch'                 : 56   <- non-zero, so the census can see processes;
    the zero above is therefore an ABSENCE, not a blind instrument.
  python-family processes still live       : 45  (all broker/poller/skill processes, none harvest)
  processes whose CommandLine reads $null  : 214  <- INSTRUMENT LIMIT, stated: these are
    system/protected processes this account cannot read a command line for. They are inside the 555
