    zero is not hiding in them -- but a CommandLine census is never a complete census, and saying so
    is the point.

INSTRUMENT NOTE: the first write of this file listed each python process with .Substring() and threw
'You cannot call a method on a null-valued expression' on a process with a null CommandLine, truncating
the list mid-way. The counts above are computed with a null guard. A reader of that first file would
have seen a plausible, complete-looking list that was one entry short of its own stated total.
